{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>And I will make your heavens like iron and your land like copper.</b> And Moshe said the reverse of this: your heavens like copper and your land like iron (Deuteronomy 28:23). For most of the commentators agreed that this whole reproof pertains to the destruction of the First Temple, while in parashat Ki Tavo it pertains to the destruction of the Second Temple. And it is known that iron is harder than copper, and in the First Temple their principal sin was toward the heavens, through worshipping stars and constellations, as it says (Jeremiah 44:18): ״וּמִן אָז חָדַלְנוּ לְקַטֵּר לִמְלֶכֶת הַשָּׁמַיִם״ — therefore the heavens would be harder for them than the earth, as it says (Job 20:27): ״יְגַלּוּ שָׁמַיִם עֲוֹנוֹ וְאֶרֶץ מִתְקוֹמָמָה לוֹ״ — for they also corrupted their way upon the earth. But in the Second Temple they did not worship idolatry, and their principal evil was on the earth, through baseless hatred and strife that was among them, and the earth was corrupted as in the generation of the Flood; therefore the earth would be harder for them than the heavens."], :book :leviticus, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:38:46.316548790Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}